The black material is three separate ordinary groups

* G1 = C1–C2 : liberties {B1 , B2}
* G2 = B3–B4 : liberties {A3 , A4 , B2}
* G3 = A2     : liberties {A1 , A3 , B2}

B2 is the unique common liberty. After any first white point that touches the formation Black can occupy B2 and unite the three groups into

G = {A2,B2,B3,B4,C1,C2}

with the three distinct external liberties A1,A3,A4. The attacking white stone is at the same time put in atari.

* W B2 : W B2 ∼ B1 only, A2,B3,C2 are black. B B1 is legal and captures W B2. After the capture B1 joins G1 and G = {A2,B1,B3,B4,C1,C2} has liberties A1,A3,A4,B2. Replaying B2 is now suicide on A2,B1,B3,C2. No net.
* W B1 : G1 is reduced to the single liberty B2 and W B1 ∼ A1,B2. B B2 is legal, joins Z,X,Y into G with liberties A1,A3,A4 and W B1 is now in one liberty A1. B A1 captures W B1, G lives on A3,A4.
* W A4 : G2 loses A4 and keeps A3,B2. W A4 ∼ A3,A5. B B2 unites G1,G2,G3 on A1,A3,A4 and W A4 is left with A3,A5. B A3 puts W A4 in one liberty A5. No forced capture.
* W A3 : W A3 ∼ A4 only. B A4 captures W A3.
* W A1 : W A1 ∼ B1 only. B B1 captures W A1.

The white D1–D2 group has E1,E2,D3,D4 ≥3 liberties so D3 is not a self atari threat.

Hence no first white point removes all liberties from any black group and survives the connecting defence B B2 with a forced net. Black can always play B2 or the appropriate recapture of the attacking white stone and keep ≥1 liberty on A2, B3–B4 and C1–C2. In particular the alleged W B2 → B B1 → W C5/A3 continuation does not reduce the merged black formation below three liberties; after W B2 B B1 the merged group still has A1,A3,A4,B2 and A3 is not a legal killing reduction because it merely occupies one of those liberties while leaving A1,A4,B2.

No first move initiates a forced killing sequence.

