3.text:
The three black formations are ordinary and distinct

* Y = C1–C2  ∼ {B1 , B2}
* X = B3–B4  ∼ {A3 , A4 , B2}
* Z = A2     ∼ {A1 , A3 , B2}

B2 is the only common liberty of X,Y,Z. D1–D2 is white and has ≥3 liberties so D3 is not a forced self-atari. Up to symmetry the only first points that can touch the black material are A1,A3,A4,B1,B2.

* W B2. W B2 ∼ B1 only because A2,B3,C2 are black. B B1 is legal and captures W B2. After the capture
  Y = B1–C1–C2 ∼ {A1 , B2}
  Z = A2 ∼ {A1 , A3 , B2}
  X = B3–B4 ∼ {A3 , A4 , B2}
  Replaying on B2 is suicide on A2,B1,B3,C2. No black group is in 0 liberties and C5 is inside the white B5–C4–D5 wall and does not touch A4. A3 is a one-liberty play for White and is captured by B A4.
* W B1. Y is reduced to ∼{B2} and W B1 ∼ {A1 , B2}. B B2 is legal and joins Z,X,Y into
  G = {A2,B2,B3,B4,C1,C2} ∼ {A1 , A3 , A4}
  while W B1 is now ∼{A1}. B A1 removes W B1.
* W A1 ∼ B1 only. B B1 captures W A1. Y,X,Z keep B2,A3,A4.
* W A3 ∼ A4 only. B A4 captures W A3.
* W A4. X loses A4 and keeps ∼{A3 , B2}. W A4 ∼ {A3 , A5}. B B2 unites Z,X,Y on {A1 , A3 , A4} and B A3 puts W A4 in one liberty A5.

In every touching first point Black can occupy B2 or immediately recapture the attacking white stone and give the merged A2–B3–B4–C1–C2 complex the three distinct external liberties A1,A3,A4 while putting the attacking white stone in atari. The C3–C4 wall does not remove A1,A3,A4 after W B2 B B1; after the capture the three black groups still retain A1,A3,A4,B2 and any White follow-up at A3 or C5 is either self-atari or does not reduce the black liberties below three.

Hence no first white point removes all liberties from any black group and survives best Black play.

